SUMMARY:Exceptional Communicators in History & the Arts
DESCRIPTION:With Annette DeCicco\n\nA 90-minute multimedia event presenting 
 famous personalities in history and the arts who were/are outstanding 
 communicators\, some as storytellers and others who inspired through 
 brevity\, metaphor\, analogy\, and anaphora. Much of the content was based 
 on Carmine Gallo's two published novels\, The Storyteller's Secret and Five 
 Stars: The Communication Secrets to Get from Good to Excellent. I also 
 broadcast a TED Talk titled Ten Ingredients for a Meaningful 
 Conversation.\n\nThe session introduction is intended to engage the group's 
 attention right away by telling them about the stories that we all have\, 
 how to dive deep\, and how to communicate personally when appropriate. From 
 there\, the many types of stories—origin stories (Howard 
 Schultz/Starbucks)\, overcoming overwhelming odds stories (JK Rowling/Harry 
 Potter)\, and rags to riches (Alexander Hamilton and 
 Lin-Manuel).\n\n\n\n\nAnnette DeCicco is an educator with an MA in 
 Education from Seton Hall University and holds an NJ real estate broker’s 
 license. Her early career was as an instructor at Essex County College. She 
 segued into real estate as managing broker of several local real estate 
 offices\, a role she held for 25 years. She has shared her knowledge at 
 Fairleigh Dickinson U. and Rutgers U. through their programs of lifelong 
 learning.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture
UID:LibCal-10341-16805532
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16805532
END:VEVENT
