DTSTAMP:20260723T000000Z
SUMMARY:World Movie Night: It Was Just an Accident
DESCRIPTION:Watch and read your way around the world with us this summer 
 with our World Movie Night and World Literature series!\n\nPlaying in our 
 World Championship Challenge? Here's a fine Group D pick for your 
 consideration: \n\nIT WAS JUST AN ACCIDENT (2025)\ndirected by Jafar Panahi 
 (Iran)\nPG-13\, 1h 44min\n\nA mechanic is reminded of his time in an 
 Iranian prison when he encounters a man he suspects to be his jailhouse 
 tormentor. Panicked\, he rounds up a few of his fellow ex-prisoners to 
 confirm the man's identity. Written and directed by acclaimed Iranian 
 filmmaker Jafar Panahi\, the film was nominated for two Academy Awards and 
 won the Palme D'Or Award at Cannes\, the NY Film Critics Circle Award for 
 Best Director\, and the Audience Award for World Cinema at the Montclair 
 Film Festival.
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 2\, West Orange Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Movie
UID:LibCal-10341-16898585
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16898585
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260724T150000Z
DTEND:20260724T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260724T000000Z
SUMMARY:July Book Club: The Lantern of Lost Memories
DESCRIPTION:A book club for adults who want to read together in community. 
 We meet one Friday morning a month to chat about a title we read in 
 common.\n\n--\nSummer World Literature Series\n\nTHE LANTERN OF LOST 
 MEMORIES\nby Sanaka Hiiragi (Japan)\n\nFrom acclaimed Japanese author 
 Sanaka Hiigari comes a heartwarming\, life-affirming novel about a magical 
 photo studio\, where people go after they die to view key moments from 
 their life—and relive one precious memory before they pass into the 
 afterlife. Translated by Jesse Kirkwood.\n\n** Participating in the World 
 Championship Challenge? Read this book as your Group D pick\, and let us 
 know how it fares in your tournament bracket! **\n\nCopies available at the 
 Circulation Desk starting June 26.
LOCATION:Literacy Room\, West Orange Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-10341-16592609
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16592609
END:VEVENT
